WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.180
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:13.639
Today we are going to see how NVIDIA’s new
AI transfers real objects into a virtual world.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:16.470
So, what is going on here?

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:22.770
Simple, in goes just one image, or a set of
images of an object.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:30.510
And the result is that an AI really transfers
this real object into a virtual world almost

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.840
immediately.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.920
Now that sounds like science fiction, how
is that even possible?

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:43.289
Well, with this earlier work, it was possible
to take a target geometry from somewhere,

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:49.129
and obtain a digital version of it by growing
it out of nothing.

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:52.780
This work reconstructed its geometry really
well.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.729
But, geometry only.

00:00:55.729 --> 00:01:02.399
This other work tried to reconstruct not just
the geometry, but everything.

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:05.190
For instance, the material models too.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:11.390
Now, incredible as this work is, it is still
baby steps in this area.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:17.520
As you see, both the geometry and the materials
are still quite coarse.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.340
So, is that it then?

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.679
Is the transferring real objects into virtual
worlds dream dead?

00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:26.369
It seems so.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:27.520
Why?

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.799
Because we either have to throw out the materials
to get a high-quality result, or if we wish

00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:38.670
to get everything, we have to be okay with
a coarse result.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.649
But, I wonder, can this be improved somehow?

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:45.880
Well, let’s find out together.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.670
And, here it is!

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.100
NVIDIA’s new work tries to take the best
of both worlds.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.399
What does that mean?

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:57.290
Well, they promise to reconstruct absolutely
everything.

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:04.649
Geometry, materials, and even the lighting
setup, and all of this with high fidelity.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:12.209
Well, that sounds absolutely amazing, but,
I will believe it when I see it!

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:14.140
Let’s see together.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.819
Well, that’s not quite what we are looking
for, is it.

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:22.420
Yes, this isn’t great, but, this is just
the start.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:30.580
Now, hold on to your papers and marvel at
how the AI improves this result over time.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.230
Oh yes, this is getting better.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.819
And, my goodness!

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:42.260
After just as little as two minutes, we already
have a usable model.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.620
That is so cool!

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.270
I love it.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:51.470
We go on a quick bathroom break and the AI
does all the hard work for us.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.470
Absolutely amazing.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:55.120
And, it gets even better!

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:03.349
Well, if we are okay with not a quick bathroom
break, but taking a nap, we get this just

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.220
an hour later.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.470
And if that is at all possible, it gets even
better than that!

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.700
How is it possible?

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:17.490
Well, imagine that we have a bunch of photos
of a historical artifact, and, you know what’s

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.490
coming!

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:25.140
Of course, creating a virtual version of it,
and dropping it into a physics simulation

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:33.110
engine, where we can edit this material, or
embed it into a cloth simulation.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.069
How cool is that?

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:37.920
And, I can’t believe it!

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.069
It still doesn’t stop there.

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:45.519
We can even change the lighting around it
and see what it would look like in all its

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:47.129
glory.

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:50.210
That is absolutely beautiful.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.210
Loving it.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:57.840
And, if we have a hot dog somewhere, and we
already created a virtual version of it, but

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.019
now, what do we do with it?

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:05.719
Of course, we engage in the favorite pastime
of the computer graphics researcher.

00:04:05.719 --> 00:04:08.840
That is, throwing jelly boxes at it.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.049
And, with this new technique, you can do that
too.

00:04:12.049 --> 00:04:20.160
And, even better, we can take an already existing
solid object and reimagine it as if it were

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.160
made of jelly.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.570
No problem at all.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.590
And, you know what - it is final boss time.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:30.580
Let’s not just reconstruct an object.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.850
Why not throw an entire scene at the AI.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.440
See if it buckles.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.420
Can it deal with that?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.690
Let’s see.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:44.570
And…I cannot believe what I am seeing here.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:51.320
It resembles the original reference scene
so well, even when animated, that it is almost

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.700
impossible to find any differences.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.100
Have you found any?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:01.120
I have to say I doubt that, because I have
swapped the labels.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:07.200
Oh yes, this is not the reconstruction, this
is the real reconstruction.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:13.320
This will be an absolutely incredible tool
in democratizing creating virtual worlds and

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.070
giving it into the hands of everyone.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.990
Bravo NVIDIA.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.220
So, what do you think?

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.130
Does this get your mind going?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.580
What else could this be useful for?

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.050
What do you expect to happen a couple more
papers down the line?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.140
Please let me know in the comments below.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:55.120
I’d love to hear 

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:22.580
your thoughts.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:32.699
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

